-- ============================================================
-- UniDesk — Complete Seed Data (live project snapshot)
-- Run AFTER schema.sql
--
-- Includes: 7 departments, 14 categories, 23 users, 200 pre-provisioned
-- student IDs (STU-2024-001..200 — the first 16 already claimed by the
-- seeded student accounts, the rest available for new self-registrations),
-- 16 student academic profiles (fees + exam records), 68 tickets with full
-- comment/status-history threads, 16 welfare cases, 5 announcements, and
-- notification preferences — reflecting realistic Sri Lankan
-- private-university demo content (not just placeholder data).
--
-- Default accounts (Passwords: Student@1 / Staff@1 / Admin@1234):
--   Admin          : admin@unidesk.edu / Admin@1234
--   Management     : management@unidesk.edu / Admin@1234
--   Help Desk      : helpdesk@unidesk.edu / Staff@1
--   Welfare        : welfare@unidesk.edu / Staff@1
--   Finance Staff  : finance@unidesk.edu / Staff@1
--   IT Staff       : itstaff@unidesk.edu / Staff@1
--   Exam Staff     : examstaff@unidesk.edu / Staff@1
--   Students (16)  : student@unidesk.edu, sarah@unidesk.edu, michael@unidesk.edu,
--                    emma@unidesk.edu, david@unidesk.edu, priya@unidesk.edu,
--                    sahan@unidesk.edu, rashmi@unidesk.edu, dinuka@unidesk.edu,
--                    nethmi@unidesk.edu, isuru@unidesk.edu, chamodi@unidesk.edu,
--                    bhanuka@unidesk.edu, kaveesha@unidesk.edu, malith@unidesk.edu,
--                    ashan@unidesk.edu (all: Student@1)
--
-- All seeded users have email_verified = 1 (they're trusted demo accounts).
-- Any NEW self-registration via /register must use one of the unclaimed
-- student IDs (STU-2024-017 through STU-2024-200) and will require clicking
-- an emailed verification link before it can log in — see
-- migration_student_registration_gate.sql and AuthService.register().
--
-- NOTE: file attachments (ticket/welfare) are intentionally excluded —
-- the physical files aren't portable across machines. Notifications,
-- the audit log, and email verification tokens are also excluded; they
-- regenerate naturally as the app is used (the overdue-ticket scheduler
-- will populate fresh notifications for any tickets that are actually
-- overdue relative to the machine's current date).
-- ============================================================

